    "faqs": [
      {
        "id": "faq-1",
        "visible": true,
        "question": "Do you really serve ONLY Tea (Chai) and Coffee?",
        "answer": "Yes! We are proudly dedicated 100% to India’s love for authentic chai and freshly brewed coffee — no snacks, no burgers, no distractions. Focusing exclusively on 12 traditional Indian teas and 10 Indian coffees allows us to freshly pound our spices, boil real kulhad batches, and drip authentic brass-filter decoction all day."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-2",
        "visible": true,
        "question": "How does the Reach & Earn Chai Coins program work?",
        "answer": "Join the free Daily Tapri Club to receive your personal invite link. Every chai or coffee you order earns Chai Coins (250 Coins = any complimentary handcrafted cup). Whenever a friend claims their free welcome chai or filter coffee via your link, you immediately receive 125–250 Coins plus up to ₹150 in instant café credit depending on your plan."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-3",
        "visible": true,
        "question": "Are your terracotta Kulhads single-use and eco-friendly?",
        "answer": "Yes! Every Kulhad Chai and Tandoori Chai is served in freshly kiln-fired, single-use natural clay kulhads sourced directly from traditional Indian potter families. They are 100% plastic-free, biodegradable, and impart that unmistakable earthy aroma."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-4",
        "visible": true,
        "question": "How authentic is your South Indian Filter Coffee?",
        "answer": "We roast Chikmagalur peaberry and plantation arabica beans blended at the classic 80% coffee to 20% chicory ratio, slow-dripped in traditional brass filters, and pulled high into boiling whole milk inside a davara-tumbler set for natural thick froth."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-5",
        "visible": true,
        "question": "Can I customize sugar, jaggery (gud), or milk strength?",
        "answer": "Absolutely. Every cup can be prepared kadak (extra strong), kam cheeni (less sugar), bina cheeni (zero sugar), or sweetened with organic palm jaggery (gud). Simply mention your preference in the barista note when ordering."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-6",
        "visible": true,
        "question": "Can I pause or cancel my Chai & Kaapi Pass anytime?",
        "answer": "Yes — zero lock-in commitments. Pause while travelling or switch back to the free Daily Tapri Club anytime while keeping all your earned Chai Coins intact."
      }
    ],
